35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the firms flagged clay and slippage, but only for deep digging. Shallow work is fine. @Minako, the depot says we can hoard the south, but not the centre.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the drainage data is grim. Callouts doubled, and heat is spiking. @Minato, the crossing counts show people strictly need firm, open ground.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, that is worrying. I found the staff is down to seven, but two volunteer groups help on weekends. I hope that is enough.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the data is clear. The basin survived, but the apron failed. @Minato, the planting record shows half died from lack of aftercare. We must judge by reality, not drawings.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the ledger confirms my fear: planted ground costs triple to maintain. @Benjamin, the fund only pays for planting, not surfacing. We must budget for the gap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Minako"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that is scary. If people need firm ground, maybe we should avoid deep digging? @Minato, are the volunteers strong enough for heavy work?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, avoid deep digging? The data says the ground is already failing. We need a plan that respects the firm paths people actually use, not just avoids the clay.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Kenji, I am not sure. The volunteers are kind, but the staff is very small. I worry they will get tired.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The apron failed because we ignored the ground. We must choose a plan that survives the weather, not just the ribbon cutting.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The fund covers planting, but the ledger shows that costs triple. We must ensure the city can afford the upkeep, not just the build.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But if we dig deep, the clay might slip. @Minako, the depot says the south is safe to hoard. Can we build there?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the south is viable, but the crossing data is the constraint. We need firm, open ground for the tram route, not just a buildable zone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I worry about the staff. With only seven people, can they handle the extra work? The volunteers help, but I am scared they will get tired.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, the volunteers are a start, but the staff gap is real. @Benjamin, the planting record proves we cannot ignore aftercare. We need a plan that survives the weather, not just the ribbon cutting.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the staff gap is real, but the ledger shows the true cost. We must pick a plan the city can actually afford to keep, not just build.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree. The clay is risky, but the depot notes say the south is safe. Maybe we can build there without deep digging?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, the south is buildable, but the crossing data is the real constraint. We need firm, open ground for the tram route, not just a buildable zone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@Benjamin, I am still worried. With only seven staff, who will mow the grass or clean the paths every single day?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
